  "summary": null,
  "thumbnail_url": null,
  "body": "<p>You can disable Discord's auto-embed feature at any time through your User Settings.</p>\n<p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"><strong>1.</strong> Click the <strong>User Settings</strong> cog icon in the bottom left corner</span></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/article_attachments/215531007/user_settings.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\"><strong>2.</strong> Select the \"<strong>Text &amp; Images</strong>\" Tab. </span><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Then, un-check the boxes titled:<br>1) \"<em>When posted as links to chat</em>.\" and <br>2) \"<em>When upload directly to Discord.</em>\"</span></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/article_attachments/360058110452\" alt=\"Capture56.jpg\"></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h3>\n<span class=\"wysiwyg-color-black\"><strong>Pro Tip</strong></span>: If you want to cancel an embed for one specific link, you can wrap the link in '<span class=\"wysiwyg-color-blue\"><strong>&lt; &gt;</strong></span>' tags.</h3>\n<p>Before:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/article_attachments/215494108/sansbrackets.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p> After:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/en-us/article_attachments/215531027/conbrackets.png\" alt=\"\"></p>",
  "body_hash": "867bacae163adae5441497de4bc46677b8dab55199713debceafaa1d37d0e8e3",
